# Foreman runtime state is local orchestration metadata, not project source.
.foreman/

# Anything that could carry a Bluetooth address, a serial, a device name with
# an embedded identifier, a host address, or a raw BLE capture.  Nothing under
# .private/ is ever publishable; see docs/SAFETY.md for the rule.
.private/
captures/
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.btsnoop
*.raw

# Scan and probe reports are runtime state.  Even the sanitized ones go stale
# the moment the radio environment changes, and the unsanitized ones must not
# exist outside .private/.  docs/EVIDENCE.md is the curated, publishable form.
reports/
*.report.json

# Python bytecode and tool caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# Collector state and local history.  state.json is sanitized, but the
# schema-2 document beside it carries the detector's heading, speed and
# altitude, and the history database can carry coordinates when the operator
# turns that on.  A rough trace of a drive must not be committable, and
# `git add -A` during a debugging session on the node is the realistic way
# that would happen.
.state/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
